{"term":"casualty","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:bfc42a930007d83dab","definition":"Something that happens by chance, especially an unfortunate event; an accident, a disaster.","example":"1756, Samuel Johnson, “The Life of Sir Thomas Browne” in Thomas Browne, Christian Morals, 2nd edition, London: J. Payne, p. xx,\nThe course of his education was like that of others, such as put him little in the way of extraordinary casualties.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fortune"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["CASEVAC","casualty department","casualty event","casualty insurance","casualty notification","casualty of superiority","casualty ward","simulated casualty"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casualty#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c1cf18f07290da54b2","definition":"A person suffering from injuries or who has been killed due to an accident or through an act of violence.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["luck"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["CASEVAC","casualty department","casualty event","casualty insurance","casualty notification","casualty of superiority","casualty ward","simulated casualty"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casualty#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9b735abbded006c318","definition":"Specifically, a person who has been killed (not only injured) due to an accident or through an act of violence; a fatality.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["luck"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"proscribed","register":"countable, proscribed, uncountable","wordFamily":["CASEVAC","casualty department","casualty event","casualty insurance","casualty notification","casualty of superiority","casualty ward","s